{"schemaVersion":1,"jobId":"map-5d5d39bb5593d8f3","runId":"ai-map-4c1-full-corpus-v1","corpusContentHash":"365e4b459f76766c2a6be5357aba61e1467a754a4aa0cb5724c1a2df2e732fb5","inputHash":"f7981d92308c7d2c8890b223f6bd1b5ba7bc61fcbecfb43cf00bbd3dd63cd33e","promptSpecVersion":"study-map-v3","disposition":"standalone","confidence":"high","reason":"Section 48 is a coherent authorization and compensation mechanism for using underground storage facilities under Board order.","proposedGroups":[{"groupId":"g1","titleSuggestion":"Board authorization and compensation for underground storage use","sourceKeys":["section:48"],"focusSelections":[{"sourceKey":"section:48","childLabels":["48(1)","48(2)","48(3)"],"evidenceText":["Board may by order authorize a person to inject gas","shall make to the owners of any gas or oil rights","No action or other proceeding lies for compensation"]}],"reason":"The subsections work together by authorizing storage use, requiring compensation to affected rights and land owners, and assigning compensation disputes to the Court of King's Bench.","approximateLearningGoal":"Recall how Board authorization for underground gas storage use connects to compensation duties and court determination of disputed compensation."}],"warnings":[],"suggestedPriority":"P1"}
